//! The `animation-range` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS)
//! [shorthand](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Cascade/Shorthand_properties)
//! property is used to set the start and end of an animation's attachment range along its timeline,
//! i.e., where along the timeline an animation will start and end.
//!
//! Initial: animation-range-start: normal; animation-range-end: normal. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: Relative to the specified named timeline range if specified, otherwise relative to
//! the entire timeline.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - normal: Represents the start of the timeline. This is the default value. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/animation-range-start
//!
//! Grammar: [ <'animation-range-start'> <'animation-range-end'>? ]#
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/scroll-animations-1/#propdef-animation-range
//!
//! Author guide:
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/animation-range
